Unofficial Offline Quranic Arabic Corpus Tool

This repository contains an unofficial, community-built tool for local offline
study workflows related to the Quranic Arabic Corpus.

This project is not produced, endorsed, reviewed, or maintained by the Quranic
Arabic Corpus project, Kais Dukes, the University of Leeds, quran.com, or any
associated maintainers.

Attribution:

- Quranic Arabic Corpus: https://corpus.quran.com
- Kais Dukes and Quranic Arabic Corpus contributors
- Language Research Group, University of Leeds
- Tanzil Project for Quranic text provenance
- Translation and annotation rights holders represented on the Corpus website
- quran.com maintainers where relevant to current hosting

This repository contains original source code and a tiny sample morphology file
for testing. It does not include the full morphology file, a SQLite database,
cached website pages, translations, images, or other third-party Corpus content.

